Negative control for the manager's form-slot clear on re-read (B2, FE-3029).

Spec that must flip: a prover spec on `#loading` entry asserting that
`context.cancellation` and `context.consolidation` are both `undefined` once
the machine re-enters `loading` (a successful form submit, `REFRESH`, or
`reset()`), even though neither `CANCEL.CANCELLATION` nor
`CANCEL.CONSOLIDATION` fired.

Mutation: `loading`'s `entry` drops `clearCancellation` and
`clearConsolidation`, leaving only `clearContractProduct`. An open form's
slot then survives a re-read: after a successful submit the manager re-places
`available` with the product re-read, but the old form (its old model) stays
on context, so a page drawing it on slot truthiness keeps showing a dead form
next to the re-shown "open" control.

